# new auto-teardown tests (tests/fm-pr-check-security.test.sh)
ok - the watcher attempts guarded cleanup only after a finished merge and surfaces its refusal reason
ok - merged notices auto-clean only finished direct reports with recorded deliverables, leave no retired task state, and surface guarded refusals without force
ok - a merge this home performs itself runs the guarded cleanup of a finished direct report and publishes its outcome durably
ok - a cleanup keeps the merge identity durable, so a late duplicate report cannot overwrite the cleanup notice
# branch prompt carve-out test (tests/fm-branch-supervision.test.sh)
ok - branch prompt is byte-stable across homes, cwd, timezone, and time, above the cache floor
